  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the historical photograph of two Black men",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the two Black men in the historical photograph. The meme's text 'the first one can't sing when you put chains on it' implicitly positions the viewer as someone who understands the historical context of chains and slavery, and thus is expected to recognize the racist stereotype being invoked. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the entire scene and the punchline are framed as a question directed at the viewer to 'get it', making the viewer the implied audience and participant in the racist joke. The projection is onto the 'two_men' entity, as the joke's punchline relies on the viewer's recognition of the historical oppression symbolized by the chains and the dehumanizing comparison to the men.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
